{"availability":"available","full":"ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-","name":"pixelforge-image-restoration-","description":"Self-trained PyTorch models for single-image super-resolution and low-light enhancement - a full pipeline from data to training, evaluation, TorchScript export, FastAPI backend and an interactive web demo.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-14T09:31:06Z","updated":"2026-10-08T11:41:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hddzzb68eqfnoed8zsmgqp.streamlit.app/","topics":["computer-vision","deep-learning","fastapi","image-restoration","low-light-enhancement","nextjs","pytorch","streamlit","super-resolution","torchscript"],"demo":"https://pixelforge-image-restoration.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.443Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.443Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.443Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.443Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PixelForge: an end-to-end image restoration pipeline","Self-trained PyTorch models for single-image super-resolution and low-light enhancement, built end to end from data to training, evaluation and deployment."],"features":["Real modelling: SRCNN, an SRResNet generator with PixelShuffle + residual blocks, and a low-light U-Net with skip connections, all written from scratch.","Full training loop: data loading, Adam + cosine annealing + AMP mixed precision + optional VGG perceptual loss, PSNR/SSIM evaluation, TorchScript export.","Three shipped weights: SR ×4 (PSNR 27.47), SR ×2 (PSNR 32.35) and low-light (PSNR 18.32) — each beats its classical baseline; classical methods remain as automatic fallback if a weight is ever missing.","Quantitative comparison: classical baselines vs. self-trained models on the same validation set; scripts and per-epoch logs are committed and recomputable.","Engineering: CI runs the tests behind a coverage gate, audits dependencies, and builds the frontend; the Docker image runs as a non-root user; the API enforces per-IP rate limiting and ships documentation."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"151065ec931d9151fab268eb9659d50c17382090e770f15888707a4d3b0bcb99","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.515Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.515Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"PixelForge: an end-to-end image restoration pipeline","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Self-host the FastAPI backend + Next.js frontend","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The FastAPI backend (serve/app.py) and the Next.js frontend (web/) are part of the same codebase and can be self-hosted; web/ posts to serve/app.py, which picks the ML engine for a task/scale when a weight is loaded, otherwise a classical baseline.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"151065ec931d9151fab268eb9659d50c17382090e770f15888707a4d3b0bcb99","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.516Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T11:41:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ElijahZhao/pixelforge-image-restoration-/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:44.517Z","hash":"151065ec931d9151fab268eb9659d50c17382090e770f15888707a4d3b0bcb99","originalBytes":18505,"storedBytes":18505,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["demo","psnr","low-light","ssim","classical","streamlit","models","training","self-trained","data","tests","serve","